      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a108cf3c9bcae9250d85b09d65216e4c9a4c1d5edc8ba9b166d020689dfa8c74",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-46f95238a290459398b4283e1f15ccba",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, fishing continues in the Flamingo area.\n\nThe main fishing grounds are in the open ocean, where the water quickly gets deeper and large pelagic species are found, and closer to the Catalina and Brummel islands.\n\nIn deeper waters, you may catch sailfish, several species of marlin, mahi-mahi, yellowfin tuna and bigeye tuna. Around the islands, you may find wahoo, Sierra mackerel, Spanish mackerel, bigeye trevally, Pacific sea bass and roosterfish.\n\nOvernight stays at **Tamarindo Diria**.\n\nMeals: breakfast and lunch."
    },
